The Scale serves as the [[Judge of Ages|Judge]]'s hand as it seeks to impose order and balance across Færrin. The seat of the Scale's power is their Stronghold -- a citadel in the Opaline Mountains that sits on a conjunction of leylines.

It was founded by [[People/Culoum Honor-Sworn|Culoum Honor-Sworn]], a companion of [[Divinity/Hierophant|Aurelia I]] who brought the first knights and mages to the Opaline Mountains. The Scale operates as an extranational form of governance with stronger guarantees than any nation could provide. The organization is split into the following groups, in order of rarity:

- **Pactbrokers** oversee contracts between parties, ensuring that both sides hold up their end, no matter what.
- **Arbiters** track down those who have escaped justice and deliver them their due.
- **Overseers** stop those seeking to seal the Gods away again, returning the planet to the Dark Ages.
- **Timekeepers** prevent meddling with the time stream, preventing the creation of paradoxes.

The average person would be most familiar with the Pactbrokers -- in most cities, one can find a member of the Scale who will (for a fee) witness the signing of a contract. Magic imbued in the contract will monitor the signees, and deviating from one's responsibilities will bring the full might of the Scale down on the contract-breaker.

Unlike many organisations that farm such work out to independent contractors, [[Org/The Scale/index|The Scale]] keeps its bounty hunting strictly in-house — only its own arbiters are empowered to pursue and recover marks.

When something strange appears, the Scale tries to be first on the scene, either to take whatever is behind it for study or to remove it before anyone else can. For the worst of these, the Scale keeps delving specialists: high-ranking members who are used to anomalies and to handling them.

The Scale is led by a tribunal, powerful people ordained with true blessings from the [[Judge of Ages|Judge]], whom high-ranking members rarely meet. Its High Arbiter is [[People/Farrow Cross|Farrow Cross]].

Within its upper ranks the Scale is split between the Puritans, who hold that the weapons of an enemy are the enemy's weapons, and the reformists, who would make use of whatever tools come to hand. Custode [[Org/The Scale/People/Macarius Vesper|Macarius Vesper]], the Scale's second in command, heads the Puritans; the head of the arbiters sits on the reformist side.

A party of Scale delvers brought the [[Org/The Scale/Voice of Many|Voice of Many]], a [[Hearts|Heart]], out of [[Sigzil Haight]]'s demesne and back to the stronghold, where it is now under the Scale's employ.

A troop of Scale delvers under [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|overseer Ralph Bishop]] has set up a forward base aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], a squat bunker of patterned concrete with a turning sonar dish on its roof. Its [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]], [[Org/The Scale/Asteris Lux|Asteris Lux]], can reach its fellows back at the stronghold over the skein.
